    <div class="content">
        <h1 id="introduction">Introduction</h1>
<p>Modular Laravel 12 API with JSON:API 5.x specification for enterprise ERP/CRM applications.</p>
<aside>
    <strong>Base URL</strong>: <code>http://localhost</code>
</aside>
<pre><code>Welcome to the ERP API documentation. This API follows the **JSON:API 1.1 specification** and provides comprehensive endpoints for:

- **Product Management** - Products, Categories, Brands, Units, Variants
- **Inventory** - Warehouses, Stock, Batches, Movements, Cycle Counts
- **Sales** - Orders, Shipments, Backorders, Discount Rules
- **Purchase** - Suppliers, Purchase Orders
- **Finance** - AR/AP Invoices, Payments, Bank Accounts
- **Accounting** - Accounts, Journal Entries, Fiscal Periods
- **HR** - Employees, Attendance, Payroll, Leave Management
- **CRM** - Leads, Campaigns, Activities, Opportunities
- **Ecommerce** - Carts, Checkout, Wishlists, Reviews
- **Billing** - CFDI Invoices, PAC Integration

&lt;aside&gt;All requests must include proper **Content-Type** and **Accept** headers: `application/vnd.api+json`&lt;/aside&gt;</code></pre>

        <h1 id="authenticating-requests">Authenticating requests</h1>
<p>To authenticate requests, include an <strong><code>Authorization</code></strong> header with the value <strong><code>"Bearer Bearer {YOUR_API_TOKEN}"</code></strong>.</p>
<p>All authenticated endpoints are marked with a <code>requires authentication</code> badge in the documentation below.</p>
<p>Authenticate using Laravel Sanctum. POST to <code>/api/auth/login</code> with email and password to get a Bearer token.</p>

        <h1 id="endpoints">Endpoints</h1>

    

                                <h2 id="endpoints-GETapi-v1-profile">GET api/v1/profile</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>



<span id="example-requests-GETapi-v1-profile">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request GET \
    --get "http://localhost/api/v1/profile" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer Bearer {YOUR_API_TOKEN}" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/vnd.api+json" \
    --header "Accept: application/vnd.api+json"</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://localhost/api/v1/profile"
);

const headers = {
    "Authorization": "Bearer Bearer {YOUR_API_TOKEN}",
    "Content-Type": "application/vnd.api+json",
    "Accept": "application/vnd.api+json",
};

fetch(url, {
    method: "GET",
    headers,
}).then(response =&gt; response.json());</code></pre></div>

</span>

